    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T21:04:11Z",
    "body": "The maintainer added this to the issue in chat on 2026-11-15.\n\nHis words: \"the tool catalog should be searchable.. By picking a tool type from dropdown, or enter name and it \"filters\" the current catalog accordingly..\"\n\nAddition to the scope, for the new catalog panel:\n\n1. The catalog panel has a tool type dropdown. Its first entry shows all types. A selected type shows only the tools of that type.\n2. The catalog panel has a text field for the name. The list shows only the tools whose name contains the text. The match ignores the letter case.\n3. The two filters apply together, and they apply to the catalog that is open.\n4. The filter text and the selected type are ephemeral UI state. They are not commands and they are not saved in the project.\n5. A filter with no match shows an empty list with a short message. It does not change the catalog.\n\nDone means, in addition to the list in the issue body:\n\n- A structural test pins the two filters: the type dropdown, the name field, the two together, and the empty result.\n\nThe claim on this issue stays with its claimant. If the work on the panel is too far to take this in, say so here, and a follow-up issue takes the search.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
